-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Nemesis the Warlock
  Publisher   Martech, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch
  (one of these files):

  File        Nemesis the Warlock (1987)(Erbe Software)[re-release].tap
  MD5         92c3a90ca49b758552374587720e700e

  File        Nemesis the Warlock (1987)(Erbe Software)[a][re-release].tzx
  MD5         ac873695b06488f3dc573d20798e1132

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Note        Keys: on the menu 1, 2 or 3 picks a control set, 4 defines keys,
              5 starts. Nemesis, the creatures and the shots are hardware
              sprites, so they no longer take the colours of the scenery they
              cross; the scenery and the panel stay as the game draws them.
              The Erbe re-release, from its tape. Proven on a long recorded
              game; later levels and the define-keys screen are not in it.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite energy
   2  Infinite bullets
   3  Infinite acid
   4  No torquemada's influence

  From an archive .pok for this re-release, each checked against its code: the
  energy subtraction, the bullet count's decrement, the acid flag and
  Torquemada's two counters. Not played.

